From 66839062c4b54cbb9acd09cb5d69fd4e01fa2e00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sachin Saxena <sachin.saxena@nxp.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 14:39:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Introduce serve_linux_stream_dpdk with RoCEv2 and
 integrate DPDK for I/O

    - Adds new serve_linux_stream_dpdk application
    - Implemented DPDK-based fast data-path for packet handling
    - Updated build and integration hooks for the new DPDK app
    - Removed CUDA emulation requirement from the build path
    - Attach cacheable camera buffers as rte_mbuf external buffers
    - Update TX fast-path to use zero-copy
    - TX/RX checksum offload
    - Introduce -DENABLE_ROCEV2=OFF option in cmake. TBD
    - ISI read uses FRAME & LINE Ready Status to avoid corruption.
    - User can control CPU cores to be use for control and data path

Signed-off-by: Gagandeep Singh <g.singh@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: Sachin Saxena <sachin.saxena@nxp.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX95 board BSP specific]
